INT. DEEP-SEA HABITAT "ABYSSAL FIVE," COMMAND CABIN - NIGHT

A cramped steel cylinder lined with gauges. A single porthole shows blackness lit by the drifting glow of jellyfish. A radio crackles on a bracket over the main console.

CAPTAIN OKONJO ADEYEMI, fifties, sits at the console with his hand hovering over a red switch. BIRGIT SOLBERG, thirties, the geologist, floats against a bulkhead, her face lit green by a monitor. RAVI NAIR, twenties, the comms tech, kneels by an open panel with a soldering iron.

                    OKONJO
          How long until the pressure seal gives?

                    BIRGIT
          Nine minutes. Maybe ten.

                    RAVI
          I can reroute the main to the secondary.

                    OKONJO
          Then do it.

He sparks the iron and hunches. She watches the gauge. The radio hisses.

                    SURFACE (V.O.)
          Abyssal Five, this is Surface Control. Do you read?

Okonjo grabs the mic.

                    OKONJO
          Surface, Okonjo. We read you.

                    SURFACE (V.O.)
          Captain, we are seeing a pressure anomaly on your hull. Advise.

                    OKONJO
          We know. We're working it.

                    SURFACE (V.O.)
          Recommend immediate ascent.

                    BIRGIT
          Ascent? That's three hours of decompression.

                    OKONJO
          Surface, negative on ascent. We're working it.

The hull groans. A rivet pops and rolls across the deck, ringing. Ravi's iron hovers over the circuit board.

                    RAVI
          Almost. Almost.

He touches the iron down. A bright blue arc snaps. The lights flicker, hold, and steady. The groaning stops. The gauge needle sinks slowly out of the red.

                    BIRGIT
          It's holding.

                    SURFACE (V.O.)
          Abyssal Five, do you copy? We show pressure normalizing.

Okonjo lets out a breath so long it fogs the glass of a dial. Ravi sits back on his heels and laughs, high and cracked. Birgit presses a palm to the bulkhead and shuts her eyes.

                    OKONJO
          Surface, Abyssal Five. We copy. Stand by.

He releases the key. The radio hisses. Silence fills the cabin, filled only by the soft tick of cooling metal.
